      "proposed_content": "Finite verification has different force depending on the unseen tail: Lagarias closes a finite prefix only after a universal analytic envelope controls every larger input; Baez-Duarte computations may miss a hypothetically delayed off-line-zero contribution; and the Nicolas argument lacks even an effective one-sided estimate from which finite checking could inherit a tail guarantee.",
