      "proposed_content": "For an integrable positive random variable, expectation of its fractional-part dilation is the negative Muntz transform of its survival function; under good-kernel regularity, this places a probability-derived deterministic kernel inside the earlier sum-integral and pseudo-convolution representation, while moments separately control Hilbert membership and tails.",
